# Architecture Kit ({{projectName}})

This repo uses **@folklore-digital/architecture-kit** (public npm package).

- **Default:** `node_modules/@folklore-digital/architecture-kit` — install with `npm i -D @folklore-digital/architecture-kit` (no PAT)
- **Local kit dev:** `export ARCHITECTURE_KIT_LOCAL=1` → uses `../architecture-kit` first

- Config: `architecture.config.json`
- Docs source: `docs/architecture/`, `docs/adr/`, `docs/diagrams/`
- Docs site (built): `public/architecture/` → served at `/architecture/` (Next.js embed)
- AI entrypoint: `docs/architecture/ai-context.md`
- Agent pack (after `scan` or site build): `.architecture-kit/agent-pack.json`

## Commands

```bash
npx architecture-kit scan              # AI bootstrap context → .architecture-kit/agent-context.md
npx architecture-kit bootstrap --apply # scaffold missing docs + merge detected config
npx architecture-kit validate          # links, mermaid, placeholders, integrations
npx architecture-kit doctor
npx architecture-kit mcp                 # MCP stdio server — see templates/mcp/README.md
npx architecture-kit dev                 # local docs site with search + dates
```

Optional Storybook: set `"storybook": { "enabled": true, "url": "..." }` in `architecture.config.json` only when the project uses Storybook.

Kit releases: bump version + tag in **architecture-kit** only. Host repos pick up new tags via semver on build.

## Scope hints for agents

- Kit/template/validator changes → **architecture-kit** repo (release new version)
- Application code → **this project** repo
- Say explicitly when a task is docs-only vs code-only
